<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01NL">Example <span data-tag="01NL">2.2.4.10</span> <span class="named">(Algebras as Lax Functors)</span>.</a> Let $[0]$ denote the category having a single object and a single morphism, which we regard as a (strict) bicategory, and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be any bicategory. Combining Remark <a data-tag="00F8" href="/tag/00F8">2.2.4.9</a> and Example <a data-tag="00DW" href="/tag/00DW">2.1.5.21</a>, we deduce that lax functors $[0] \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ can be identified with pairs $(Y, A)$, where $Y \in \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is an object and $A$ is an algebra object of the monoidal category $\underline{\operatorname{End}}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}(Y)$. </p>
</article>
